Include <unistd.h> in the bundled libzip mkstemp, the way php-src does from 7.2.

ext/zip/lib/mkstemp.c calls getpid() with no declaration in scope. clang 16 and
newer make -Wimplicit-function-declaration an error by default, so the bundled
libzip that --enable-zip builds on these branches does not compile:

  error: call to undeclared function 'getpid'; ISO C99 and later do not support
  implicit function declarations

php-src added the include in 7.2 (guarded for Windows, which has no unistd.h);
7.2 and 7.3 already carry it. This is that guard, in the same place, with the
same shape.

This is exactly the diagnostic php/build.sh deliberately re-promotes to an
error for `make` after demoting it for `./configure` -- and it is the reason
that split is worth having. An implicitly declared getpid() returns int, which
on LP64 truncates nothing here only because pid_t is int; the same silence
applied to a function returning a pointer is a real bug. The right answer is
the missing include, not a wider suppression.
--- a/ext/zip/lib/mkstemp.c
+++ b/ext/zip/lib/mkstemp.c
@@ -43,6 +43,9 @@
 #endif
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#ifndef _WIN32
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
 
 #ifndef O_BINARY
 #define O_BINARY 0
